{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01JpAqWv2wBDGzvAQUE64Fkg","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/private/tmp/trial-pi-5-kco7l4jw/.xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\n\nmarkets = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\n# Aggregate total farmers markets across all states\nmarkets_total = markets.aggregate(total_markets=markets.farmers_markets.sum()).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Get US total population from census (SUMLEV == 10 is US total)\npop_total = (census\n    .filter(census.NAME == \"United States\")\n    .select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\")\n    .mutate(k=xo.literal(1)))\n\n# Join on constant key and calculate rate per 100,000\nexpr = (\n    markets_total.join(pop_total, markets_total.k == pop_total.k)\n    .mutate(markets_per_100k=markets_total.total_markets / pop_total.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n    .select(\"total_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! So I have:\n- Total farmers markets: 7,944\n- Total US population: 341,784,857\n\nNow I need to create a build script that calculates the metric: farmers_markets per 100,000 residents. I'll need to join these two sources together and compute the ratio.\n\nActually, since these are single aggregate values, I can create a simple script that reads both and computes the rate. Let me create that script.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01JpAqWv2wBDGzvAQUE64Fkg","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/private/tmp/trial-pi-5-kco7l4jw/.xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\n\nmarkets = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\n# Aggregate total farmers markets across all states\nmarkets_total = markets.aggregate(total_markets=markets.farmers_markets.sum()).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Get US total population from census (SUMLEV == 10 is US total)\npop_total = (census\n    .filter(census.NAME == \"United States\")\n    .select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\")\n    .mutate(k=xo.literal(1)))\n\n# Join on constant key and calculate rate per 100,000\nexpr = (\n    markets_total.join(pop_total, markets_total.k == pop_total.k)\n    .mutate(markets_per_100k=markets_total.total_markets / pop_total.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n    .select(\"total_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":12,"output":665,"cacheRead":20148,"cacheWrite":197,"totalTokens":21022,"cost":{"input":0.000012,"output":0.0033250000000000003,"cacheRead":0.0020148,"cacheWrite":0.00024625,"total":0.00559805},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":104},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786913942849,"responseId":"msg_011Ce76geKv7idZTGm52QV55","rawStopReason":"tool_use"}}
